mber to December has come in under 90% of normal in 39 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids, more than any other pair. In 2025, August to September ran 38% of normal and November to December 43% on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 44% and March to April at 151% on the middle of the grids. Grid 22659 had its driest year in 1953 at 58% of normal.</p>"}
